  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This brief twelve-minute audience recording captures the Mountain Goats performing on Saturday, July 18, 1992, at the Casa de Badger in Pomona [1][4]. The file, rated 4.5 out of 5 by two listeners, is the only available recording of this specific show [1]. The setlist includes five songs: Moon Song, Going to Chino, Going to Mexico, Going to Wisconsin, and In the Cane Fields [1]. Notably, Moon Song and Going to Wisconsin are the only archived performances of these tracks, while In the Cane Fields is rare with just two archived performances [1]. Going to Chino and Going to Mexico are also the earliest recordings of these songs in the archive [1]. The uploader describes this as a very early live recording from the famous Butter archives, noting it is one of the earliest Mountain Goats shows ever recorded [1]. One reviewer calls it a gem with very clean audio [2]. Another reviewer highlights that the short recording has great quality for its age, though it lacks songs the band would later become known for [3]. That same reviewer suggests Going to Mexico is the best track in this set [3]. This is the first of 467 Mountain Goats recordings in the archive's collection [4].",
